* ==================================================================
* tb_sar_logic_timing -- what the synchronous choice actually buys,
* measured rather than asserted (issue #11, DR-0008).
*
* GENERATED by design/sar-logic/flow/gen_sar_ctrl_gates_tb.py -- do not edit.
*
* ISSUE #311: this deck instantiates ONE loop of the five-loop
* family above (ok/lt/xl/bad/tie), not all five. ngspice advances
* one GLOBAL timestep for a whole deck, so five clock-sharing
* sar_ctrl_a instances sharing one file force each other's step
* down to the union of their switching activity -- measured at up
* to ~100x the cost per simulated ns of running one loop alone
* (sim/sar-logic-timing-gates/investigations/
* 20260917-issue-303-five-loop-composition-cost.md). The loops
* are electrically independent -- each has its own sar_ctrl_a
* instance, CDAC/comparator and stimulus, sharing only the `clk`
* stimulus and the `vdd_gate` supply -- so splitting them changes
* NOTHING about what is measured, only how many loops share one
* deck. The measurement definitions, bounds and 8.5 us duration
* are UNCHANGED from the five-loop composition.
*
* `ok`: 0 ns delay -- the reference point. No delay is
* inserted between the comparator's analog decision and
* the controller sampling it, so with no added decision
* delay every conversion must come out exact.
*
* ==================================================================

